{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0ed3a5f6dada7c30fad190e6409b953dac3904594f4c982c92b894d0af241f3e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"In legacy-inject mode, when memory hits its character limit the extension spawns a one-shot consolidation child process that merges entries, then reloads and retries the save; in policy-only mode SQLite is the query authority and consolidation is manual via /memory-consolidate."},{"claim_ids":["clm_11d11a9e7a75fb82606133515004e925b83d48417c6f2e400d51fb980408e806"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Standing instructions (/memory-pin) are a user-authored file injected into every session in every memory mode, capped at 20 entries / 2,000 characters, stored in STANDING.md which background processes cannot write; the feature is explicitly not tool enforcement."},{"claim_ids":["clm_174d6ccc66bb2780849db40869c7a507e5576cd8de47c0b52f2b4e43cf640d3a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"For create and update, skill_manage prefers structured fields (when_to_use, procedure_steps, pitfalls, verification_steps) rendered into SKILL.md sections, and global creation has duplicate/similarity guards blocking exact slug matches and near-name collisions."},{"claim_ids":["clm_549b4cc1458defe07304f3f91f87f8a9fa2be589e1464d010f413fa1495f0aa5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The extension manages three knowledge types: MEMORY.md facts (5,000-char cap), USER.md profile (5,000-char cap), and Pi-native SKILL.md procedures with unlimited size."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5a94283b8169a656389fee0af3cd4a261aa7698c18e07c334ad0707c65578e74"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"By default review, flush, correction save, and manual consolidation use an in-process completeSimple() side-channel, falling back to a pi -p --no-session subprocess on failure; reviewTransport can force subprocess-only behavior."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5bf8d5fecb60836b6e1d053e2ec3841f211f82ef69f3d17d804384d046475a70"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Background review triggers every 10 turns or every 15 tool calls, with both counters reset after each review; correction detection saves immediately when the user corrects the agent."},{"claim_ids":["clm_65d316b872c5828ec056e7cb0e120cb7d9a838d388c2be0335f396ee71ae598d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Recall in policy-only mode is probabilistic: a stored rule only takes effect if the agent calls memory_search before the relevant action, so prohibitions may be missed while preferences survive a missed lookup."},{"claim_ids":["clm_66ed01198b939cf0e662e3121f2f3041bd65a0d953c2f47f0f71bc8d4e4835a5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Project-scoped skills are exposed to Pi via the resources_discover hook, which returns the active project's skills directory so Pi discovers them natively without copying into the global folder."},{"claim_ids":["clm_71c1269ca8202fddf04f70b3b22db72280b795be23766a866cf9bbe9b6d514dc"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Memory is stored at two tiers: global facts under ~/.pi/agent/pi-hermes-memory/ and per-project facts under ~/.pi/agent/projects-memory/<project>/, with project memories searchable when the cwd matches."},{"claim_ids":["clm_720499bf6eb3082cf3586fdb2a464558987791b361f1c13cc447401faf30a128"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"An optional lazyInitialization mode defers Markdown/SQLite sync, memory loading, maintenance, and session indexing until the first memory operation, while pinned STANDING.md instructions and skill discovery remain available at startup; legacy-inject ignores the option."},{"claim_ids":["clm_76e9df803ff5ea59a70ef0967467ffa240b208119eb05bab76f37c58969014b5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documented limitation: the FTS5 trigram tokenizer only supports CJK substring search for terms of three or more characters; one- and two-character memory_search terms may not match."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7a9b488cd6ef4296820e19d84378c46a25e9de0be7474e2b5399c67e39398847"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"An opt-in sessionSearch.variant of 'anchors' makes session_search read session JSONL files directly and return path:startLine-endLine anchors with short reasons instead of summaries."},{"claim_ids":["clm_840b3c4c74a5ae2f348ac648de9d507d6b14ff232c355c08ccad8e9b6823f0fa"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The agent gets memory write tools memory_add, memory_replace, and memory_remove with targets memory, user, project, and failure, plus a skill_manage tool with create, view, patch, update, and delete actions."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8a0d9d2138ba89ac9efa0eb7b9b1122d1d0f01a5c2e3f9ca9486a5bbbd7ab184"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Slash commands include /memory-insights, /memory-skills, /memory-consolidate, /memory-interview, /memory-index-sessions, /memory-sync-markdown, /memory-preview-context, /memory-pin, and /learn-memory-tool."},{"claim_ids":["clm_97623f29447ae2caf1d26dfed8c6ad193480464a0fe682bc2d4815325d48ef54"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Memory blocks are wrapped in <memory-context> XML tags with a guard note stating they are not new user input, to prevent the model from treating stored facts as instructions."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d68f1b0302c53cf03ffc047b53c7189bbdd59481ef8649e35b563222ffde01be"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The extension depends on better-sqlite3, a native addon that can fail with Node ABI mismatches (e.g. Homebrew-installed Pi); it attempts one automatic npm rebuild and documents a manual rebuild path."},{"claim_ids":["clm_db4b31709c9d5819e3c3635381caf139c887469b57fba85194e2aca9e57210e7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Search tools include session_search over past conversations and memory_search over the extended store; FTS5 with a trigram tokenizer supports multi-word, quoted-phrase, OR-operator, and CJK substring queries of three or more characters."},{"claim_ids":["clm_deeb1d9cfe252fe7a36fe1ed59c9c8e77687df74ff488f6d1486bdee6e0b3dfd"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A hybrid architecture keeps Markdown as the human-readable source of truth while mirroring successful writes into a SQLite store (sessions.db) queried via memory_search; failed core writes are not silently spilled into SQLite-only storage."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e6d54ad2abe524e1dd97076f7acc92ba99b5c23b081c67117ab2d66b9828e645"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"By default full Markdown memories are not injected into the system prompt; instead a <memory-policy> block tells the agent when to call memory_search, keeping first-turn token usage low."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0ed3a5f6dada7c30fad190e6409b953dac3904594f4c982c92b894d0af241f3e","clm_11d11a9e7a75fb82606133515004e925b83d48417c6f2e400d51fb980408e806","clm_174d6ccc66bb2780849db40869c7a507e5576cd8de47c0b52f2b4e43cf640d3a","clm_549b4cc1458defe07304f3f91f87f8a9fa2be589e1464d010f413fa1495f0aa5","clm_5a94283b8169a656389fee0af3cd4a261aa7698c18e07c334ad0707c65578e74","clm_5bf8d5fecb60836b6e1d053e2ec3841f211f82ef69f3d17d804384d046475a70","clm_65d316b872c5828ec056e7cb0e120cb7d9a838d388c2be0335f396ee71ae598d","clm_66ed01198b939cf0e662e3121f2f3041bd65a0d953c2f47f0f71bc8d4e4835a5","clm_71c1269ca8202fddf04f70b3b22db72280b795be23766a866cf9bbe9b6d514dc","clm_720499bf6eb3082cf3586fdb2a464558987791b361f1c13cc447401faf30a128","clm_76e9df803ff5ea59a70ef0967467ffa240b208119eb05bab76f37c58969014b5","clm_7a9b488cd6ef4296820e19d84378c46a25e9de0be7474e2b5399c67e39398847","clm_840b3c4c74a5ae2f348ac648de9d507d6b14ff232c355c08ccad8e9b6823f0fa","clm_8a0d9d2138ba89ac9efa0eb7b9b1122d1d0f01a5c2e3f9ca9486a5bbbd7ab184","clm_97623f29447ae2caf1d26dfed8c6ad193480464a0fe682bc2d4815325d48ef54","clm_d68f1b0302c53cf03ffc047b53c7189bbdd59481ef8649e35b563222ffde01be","clm_db4b31709c9d5819e3c3635381caf139c887469b57fba85194e2aca9e57210e7","clm_deeb1d9cfe252fe7a36fe1ed59c9c8e77687df74ff488f6d1486bdee6e0b3dfd","clm_e6d54ad2abe524e1dd97076f7acc92ba99b5c23b081c67117ab2d66b9828e645"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:41:06Z","created_by_operation":"op_872da1d25964457584d7ae325047402c","id":"pg_351e253dd1205c37b83316e1773ff6f4","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/chandra447-pi-hermes-memory